## Feature #6 Increment 1 (spec §4.6) — immutable `Schedule` builder + the SYNC
## `run` driver over a `Result`-returning block.
##
## `Schedule.recurs(n)` is an immutable retry policy (n+1 total tries, no delay).
## `sched.run do … end` re-evaluates the block each attempt; on `Err` it retries
## up to the budget, returning the final `Result` (the first `Ok`, or the last
## `Err` once attempts are spent). The block is re-invoked per attempt (it must
## be `Fn`).
##
## A `Flaky` source fails (Err) the first 2 calls then succeeds Ok(99).
## `recurs(5)` (6 tries) → it succeeds on the 3rd try → `Ok(99)`. A `recurs(1)`
## (2 tries) over a source that fails 3× → exhausts → returns the last `Err`.
## Proves: the immutable builder, the sync re-invoke-and-retry loop, and that
## the budget is honoured both ways (success-within and exhaust).

class Flaky
  n: Int
  fail_until: Int
  ok_val: Int
  def init(fail_until: Int, ok_val: Int)
    self.n = 0
    self.fail_until = fail_until
    self.ok_val = ok_val
  end
  ## Err(attempt#) for the first `fail_until` calls, then Ok(ok_val).
  def var attempt -> Result[Int, Int]
    self.n = self.n + 1
    if self.n <= self.fail_until
      Result.Err(self.n)
    else
      Result.Ok(self.ok_val)
    end
  end
end

def main
  puts "sched start"

  # Succeeds on the 3rd try (fails twice), budget 6 → Ok(99).
  var a = Flaky.new(2, 99)
  var sa = Schedule.recurs(5)
  let ra = sa.run do
    a.attempt
  end
  match ra
    Ok(v)  -> puts "a_ok=#{v}"
    Err(e) -> puts "a_err=#{e}"
  end

  # Fails 3×, budget 2 (recurs(1)) → exhausts → last Err.
  var b = Flaky.new(9, 0)
  var sb = Schedule.recurs(1)
  let rb = sb.run do
    b.attempt
  end
  match rb
    Ok(v)  -> puts "b_ok=#{v}"
    Err(e) -> puts "b_err=#{e}"
  end

  puts "sched done"
end
